course: dictionary
lesson: 12390
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and cultivation is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Ask yourself which meaning fits the whole sentence best.
explain: In farming, cultivation means preparing land and growing crops or plants on it: ploughing, planting, watering and harvesting. «Land under cultivation» is land that is being farmed. «The cultivation of rice» means the growing of rice.
explain: Cultivation can also mean developing a skill, quality or friendship carefully over time. «Her cultivation of good habits» means she has been building those habits slowly, day by day. The clue is the words over time.
explain: In a formal sense, cultivation means being educated and having good manners and taste. «Her cultivation showed in her polite speech and her love of books.» Here the clues are polite and love of books, so the word is about her education and manners, not about farming.
fact: Cultivation is a noun. It names the act of cultivating, which means preparing land and growing things, or developing something carefully.
fact: «Cultivation» can mean preparing land and growing crops or plants on it.
fact: «Land under cultivation» means land that is being farmed.
fact: «Cultivation» can mean developing a skill, quality or friendship carefully over time.
fact: Long ago, people learned the cultivation of wheat and changed from hunting to farming.
exercise: «The farmer spent the spring on the cultivation of the fields: ploughing, planting and watering.» What does cultivation mean here? | Cooking food over a fire | Hunting animals in the forest | *Preparing land and growing crops on it | Painting pictures of the sky
exercise: «Years of practice helped her in the cultivation of her piano skills.» What does cultivation mean here? | Breaking the piano | Selling her piano | *Developing a skill carefully over time | Moving house
exercise: In history lessons, people learned the cultivation of which crop? | Computers | *Wheat | Bicycles | Trains
test: «The rice fields were under cultivation all year.» What does under cultivation mean? | Being sold in shops | Being covered in snow | Being closed for repairs | *Being farmed
test: «Her cultivation of good manners made her a kind and polite guest.» What does cultivation mean here? | Walking long distances | Growing vegetables in a garden | *Being educated and having good manners | Losing a game
exam: «The cultivation of good habits, like reading every night, takes time.» What does cultivation mean here? | Cutting down trees | Buying new books | *Developing good habits carefully over time | Preparing land for crops
